Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> As posted a couple days ago, my priest sacrificed as mad but
> got just a few of the crappy artifact weapons, and then at some
> point nothing more; so I suppose there may be some limit, or
> is it just a very low generation probability and I was unlucky?
>
> I decided to go with Dragonbane, enchanted it to +6, and did
> fairly well with it - there are so many dragons in UN, it seems!

Two heck^2 levels have some additional dragons but the rest AFAIR
should have the same probability for dragons as the vanilla levels.

> But a hit to a harmless looking 'v' instantly disintegrated my
> artifact weapon.[*][**]

I don't know if it's harmless looking but it should look different
than the other vortices if the dark grey patch is working on your
terminal.

> I suppose that UN behaves like Vanilla,
> and a generated and disintegrated artifact still counts in the
> sacrifice offer formula?

Yes, it's the same as in Vanilla.

> Well, so I now have to choose from one of my other weapons;
> Trollbane, Sting, Orcrist, unicorn horn, or a (restricted!)
> silver sabre. Or would it be worth continuing sacrificing for
> a better weapon?

Of those weapons Trollsbane is certainly the best. It is a bit
improved from the vanilla Trollsbane. It warns of trolls and gives you
regeneration.

